                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The Ministry of Health’s Drug Advisory Committee is unable to make a recommendation on pralsetinib for inclusion on the MOH List of Subsidised Drugs because the company has withdrawn its application from the company-led submission process due to the decision to end its global collaboration agreement to develop and commercialise pralsetinib. This submission was for treating rearranged during transfection (RET) fusion-positive, locally advanced or metastatic non-small-cell lung cancer."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
